WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.350 --> 00:00:05.300
8 actors we lost far too soon

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:09.290
Hollywood loves the young and beautiful, and
it's easy to think of our favorite stars as

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:14.109
being immortal up on the big screen. Sadly,
that isn't the case, and a number of actors

00:00:14.109 --> 00:00:19.080
have given us sobering reminders of just how
fragile life can be. Here are eight examples

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:22.530
of talented performers we lost far too soon.

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:24.120
Paul Walker

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:28.930
An action movie veteran who served as a cornerstone
of The Fast and The Furious franchise, Paul

00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:33.300
Walker had broader ambitions beyond starring
in your average action flick. He branched

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:39.899
out with projects like the Hurricane Katrina-inspired
Hours, and the ensemble comedy Pawn Shop Chronicles.

00:00:39.899 --> 00:00:44.179
There's really no telling what he might have
been able to accomplish if he'd survived the

00:00:44.179 --> 00:00:50.659
tragic car crash that took his life at the
age of 40 in November 2013.

00:00:50.659 --> 00:00:52.620
Heath Ledger

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:57.019
He may have gotten his start on Australian
television, but the first glimpse of Heath

00:00:57.019 --> 00:01:02.940
Ledger's gifts for worldwide audiences came
courtesy of the 1999 teen comedy 10 Things

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:08.000
I Hate About You. Ledger's work as the brooding
teen Patrick Verona, while certainly one of

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.509
the movie's highlights, didn't really hint
at the depth of his talent, which was only

00:01:12.509 --> 00:01:17.649
exposed after he shrugged off his shot at
Hollywood hunkdom in favor of taking on more

00:01:17.649 --> 00:01:22.920
challenging parts in pictures like Monster's
Ball and Brokeback Mountain. For many, Ledger's

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:27.390
defining role came as the Joker in The Dark
Knight, which netted him a Best Supporting

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:32.859
Actor Oscar after his shocking death of an
accidental prescription drug overdose in early

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:39.880
2008. Only 28 when he died, Ledger would certainly
have gone on to even greater things.

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:41.090
Bruce Lee

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:46.070
Martial arts legend Bruce Lee made some of
the best-loved kung fu movies of all time,

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:51.939
and he seemed like he was only getting started.
But in 1973, at the age of 32, he died of

00:01:51.939 --> 00:01:57.219
brain swelling, denying the world his gifts.
The Lee family's tragic history continued

00:01:57.219 --> 00:02:03.490
in 1993, when Lee's son Brandon was accidentally
shot and killed while filming a scene during

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:08.780
production on The Crow. Just 28 when he died,
Brandon might have taken his father's legacy

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:15.360
even further; instead, his death added another
dark chapter to an already grim story.

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:17.440
Skye McCole Bartusiak

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:21.300
Though she isn't anywhere as well-known as
some of the other names on this list, Skye

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:26.720
McCole Bartusiak compiled an incredible repertoire
of credits during her too-brief career. A

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:31.640
mere 7 years old when she booked a role in
The Cider House Rules, Bartusiak went on to

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:37.070
star alongside such famous names as Mel Gibson
in The Patriot, Michael Douglas in Don't Say

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:42.610
a Word, and Hilary Swank in a stage adaptation
of The Miracle Worker. Along the way, she

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:48.280
also appeared in a supporting role on 24 and
was nominated three times for a Young Artist

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:54.730
Award. She was only 21 when she succumbed
to an accidental drug overdose in 2014.

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:56.650
River Phoenix

00:02:56.650 --> 00:03:01.400
Getting his acting start at the tender age
of 10, River Phoenix quickly found fame through

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:06.750
memorable appearances in '80s movies like
Stand by Me and Explorers. Tempted with teen

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:12.200
idol status, Phoenix mostly avoided paycheck
roles, focusing instead on roles in films

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:17.260
like The Mosquito Coast, Little Nikita, and
Running on Empty. But while he led a serious

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:22.160
actor's life on the big screen, his personal
affairs were sadly far more stereotypical

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:27.770
for Young Hollywood. His dangerous habits
caught up with him in the fall of 1993, when

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:33.250
the 23-year-old Phoenix collapsed outside
a Los Angeles club after overdosing on multiple

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:34.290
drugs.

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:36.010
John Belushi

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:40.690
Part of what audiences loved about comic actor
John Belushi during his breakout years on

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:46.200
Saturday Night Live was his wild, untameable
image. While that manic, outsized energy was

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:51.580
great for SNL and movies like Animal House,
it was only part of a lifestyle that was far

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:57.250
too intense to last. As Belushi's stardom
continued to rise with 1980's Blues Brothers

00:03:57.250 --> 00:04:01.730
and a host of planned projects that would
have highlighted his dramatic range, his chemical

00:04:01.730 --> 00:04:06.990
indulgences continued to worsen. Despite the
best efforts of friends and loved ones concerned

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:12.760
for his well-being, Belushi succumbed to a
drug overdose in March of 1982, at the age

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:14.680
of 33.

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:16.530
Chris Farley

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:21.530
His infectious energy and ample girth provoked
plenty of John Belushi comparisons after Chris

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:26.970
Farley joined the cast of Saturday Night Live
in the spring of 1990. Sadly, the two stars

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:32.720
also shared similarities off-screen, and like
Belushi, Farley's SNL tenure was shadowed

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:37.740
by concerns for his long-term health. In spite
of his personal demons, Farley branched out

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:43.410
into a promising film career that included
the 1995 cult classic Tommy Boy—but after

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:49.250
he was fired from SNL the same year. He never
really came close to achieving his potential.

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:54.920
Like Belushi, Farley was only 33 at his time
of death, the sad result of a drug overdose

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:57.830
in December 1997.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:59.920
Philip Seymour Hoffman

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:04.639
Arguably one of the greatest actors of his
generation, Philip Seymour Hoffman carved

00:05:04.639 --> 00:05:10.139
out a solid niche for himself as one of Hollywood's
"that guy" supporting players. Eventually,

00:05:10.139 --> 00:05:15.250
Hoffman got a leg up from director Paul Thomas
Anderson, who cast him in a series of productions

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:21.700
starting with 1996's Hard Eight. As his profile
rose, Hoffman bounced between arthouse dramas,

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:26.710
mainstream comedies, and even blockbuster
action pictures like Mission: Impossible III

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:31.389
and the Hunger Games franchise. Sadly, he
also struggled with substance abuse. After

00:05:31.389 --> 00:05:37.700
more than 20 years of sobriety, he relapsed
in 2013, overdosing on a mixture of drugs

00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:41.520
early the following year, at the age of 46.

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:45.670
Thanks for watching! Subscribe to our YouTube
channel to see more videos like the one you

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:50.090
just saw. And leave us a comment to let us
know what other actors you loved that were

00:05:50.090 --> 00:05:51.389
lost far too soon...

